{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / immutable audit base\nAt d49fea41cc383dc70d465903e94598a6dc790bd1, these five files contain 36 confirmed bloated prose blocks. The former older-SHA ranges mixed executable code, section labels, directives, and concise/load-bearing docs while missing long read, ancestry, graph, and op-cert explanations. Lines are immutable-base citations only.\n\n## Exact prose allowlist\nA stable ID is the full path plus :: plus the listed suffix. Only these blocks may change.\n\n- src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py (18): module-docstring@1-22; sort_states-docstring@71-77; tracker_dir-docstring@100-110; tracker_dir::comment(A repo-root was supplied)@141-148; module::comment(Read-path reconverge waits only briefly)@160-164; _sync_disabled-docstring@210-215; ensure_fresh-docstring@225-233; ensure_fresh::comment(sync.pull and tickets.branch are code-repo config)@236-240; ensure_fresh::comment(Claim the throttle window before reconverging)@275-280; ensure_fresh::comment(Reconverge in-process)@286-290; inbound_deps_state-docstring@321-334; show_state::comment(Show emits the same compiled-state shape)@361-364; _load_scratch::comment(scratch.base_dir via typed config)@379-384; module::comment(Fields a discovery list never consumes)@416-425; lean_projection-docstring@437-443; list_states-docstring@448-463; search_state::comment(Enrich each state with its bound Jira key)@580-584; recent_session_logs_state-docstring@608-612.\n- src/rebar/attest/authorship_resolution.py (5): resolve_event_commit-docstring@11-30; resolve_position_commit-docstring@71-82; build_ticket_position_commit_map-docstring@119-154; build_introducing_commit_map-docstring@213-243; build_position_commit_map-docstring@293-315.\n- src/rebar/graph/_links.py (5): _is_active_link::comment(SNAPSHOT fallback)@92-97; _write_link_event-docstring@127-147; add_dependency-docstring@222-244; add_dependency::comment(Steps zero-one validate relation grammar)@245-251; remove_dependency-docstring@353-370.\n- src/rebar/opcert_service/app.py (3): module-docstring@1-20; lifespan::comment(An app-owned executor)@59-66; lifespan::comment(Bound the cancel and await)@77-80.\n- src/rebar/opcert_service/workspace.py (5): module-docstring@1-11; module::comment(Wall-clock bound on every git subprocess)@23-30; module::comment(Write-lock acquisition budget)@33-39; _git-docstring@60-70; _populate::comment(Converge the freshly-mounted tracker)@141-145.\n\n## Contracts, consumers, and exclusions\nPreserve the single read implementation, sort/null rules, relocated-store resolution, short-lock freshness, throttle-before-sync, inbound-edge derivation, show/list/search shape, lean omission set, filtering, Jira-key enrichment, and session-log ordering. Preserve oldest-add commit semantics, full-history/no-merge/no-rename walks, record framing, map fallback, and fail-closed resolution. Preserve link idempotency/cycle/promotion/reciprocal semantics and durable-write-before-output order. Preserve op-cert async API/authentication, app-owned executor shutdown, authoritative workspace, git/stall bounds, boot lock budget, and stripped remotes.\n\nNo allowlisted docstring is directly read via __doc__/inspect.getdoc. FastAPI does consume the decorated health/submit_job/get_job docstrings for OpenAPI; those concise docs are deliberately outside the allowlist. Preserve reads.py tickets-boundary-ok line 122 and BLE001 lines 295/297/549; authorship_resolution.py BLE001 lines 64/112/208/288/366; _links.py T201 line 258; app.py BLE001 line 202; workspace.py raw-git-ok lines 58/88. All other non-allowlisted prose, runtime strings, assertions, fixtures, decorators, subprocess arguments, config keys/values, directives, and shebangs remain byte-identical.\n\n## Verification and independent review\nUse d49fea41cc383dc70d465903e94598a6dc790bd1 only to identify and cite the 36 audited prose blocks. Parse the implementation parent (HEAD^) and final Python with type_comments=True; strip only allowlisted owner docstrings, normalize only ast.TypeIgnore.lineno, and require remaining AST/runtime equality plus directive/shebang physical-line equality. Require exact HEAD^..HEAD paths. Before push, run the focused read/ancestry/link/op-cert contracts, the exact-path diff check, comment hygiene, worktree-venv make lint, and worktree-venv make typecheck. Gerrit Verified CI supplies the full-suite gate before merge.\n\nA non-author reviewer records a leaf-linked TSV with exactly 36 PASS rows: stable_id, before_citation, final_citation, preserved_contract_or_consumer, directives_exact, before_words, final_words, reviewer_session, semantic_pass, bloat_pass. Every block must shrink.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Exactly the 36 allowlisted prose blocks are shortened.\n- [x] Every allowlisted block has a lower final word count than its cited before version.\n- [x] Every non-allowlisted docstring remains unchanged.\n- [x] Every non-allowlisted ordinary comment remains unchanged.\n- [x] Every directive and shebang physical line remains unchanged.\n- [x] The implementation-parent/final AST/runtime oracle passes for all five files.\n- [x] The implementation-parent/final ordinary-comment token oracle passes for all five files.\n- [x] Every preserved read, ancestry, graph, op-cert, and workspace contract has an independent-review PASS citation.\n- [x] HEAD^..HEAD changes exactly the five recorded file-impact paths.\n- [x] The focused contract-test command exits 0.\n- [x] The exact-path diff-check command exits 0.\n- [x] The comment-hygiene command exits 0.\n- [x] Worktree-venv make lint exits 0 before push.\n- [x] Worktree-venv make typecheck exits 0 before push.\n- [x] The independent TSV contains exactly 36 complet